### Tested versions

- Reproducible in 4.6


### System information

LinuxBSD - Godot 4.6

### Issue description

Joypad events are ignored if we build the lib as shared library

Kind of surprising that JoypadSDL member is not part of `OS` as SDL is platform independent. In any-case probably it is better of GododInstance calls a method in `OS` to process events, which in turn should dispatch the process events to display server and anything in-between.

### Steps to reproduce

- Create a godot shared library, and link with it via a launcher with this code:
```cpp

int main(int argc, char **argv) {
	// Create a Godot instance using the C API
	// This initializes Godot and the game extension
	// Pass command-line arguments directly - configure launch settings in launch.json
	GDExtensionObjectPtr godot_instance = libgodot_create_godot_instance(argc, argv, game_extension_init);

	if (godot_instance == nullptr) {
		return 1;
	}

	// Cast to GodotInstance to call methods directly
	// This is safe because we know libgodot_create_godot_instance returns a GodotInstance*
	GodotInstance *instance = reinterpret_cast<GodotInstance *>(godot_instance);

	// Start the engine
	if (!instance->start()) {
		libgodot_destroy_godot_instance(godot_instance);
		return 1;
	}

	// Main loop
	while (!instance->iteration()) {
		// Per-frame host-side work can go here
	}

	// Cleanup - uninitialize the game module first
	uninitialize_game_module();

	// Destroy the Godot instance (this also calls Main::cleanup internally)
	libgodot_destroy_godot_instance(godot_instance);

	return 0;
}

```

### Minimal reproduction project (MRP)

The issue is evident compare :
```cpp

bool GodotInstance::iteration() {
	DisplayServer::get_singleton()->process_events();
	return Main::iteration();
}
```

To:
```cpp

void OS_LinuxBSD::run() {
	if (!main_loop) {
		return;
	}

	main_loop->initialize();

	//uint64_t last_ticks=get_ticks_usec();

	//int frames=0;
	//uint64_t frame=0;

	while (true) {
		DisplayServer::get_singleton()->process_events(); // get rid of pending events
#ifdef SDL_ENABLED
		if (joypad_sdl) {
			joypad_sdl->process_events();
		}
#endif
		if (Main::iteration()) {
			break;
		}
	}

	main_loop->finalize();
}
```
